    "promptText": "Use my uploaded photo as the ONLY source of my facial identity. Recreate the reference image as closely as possible in composition, framing, poses, clothing, lighting, colours, filter, texture and photographic mood. The reference person's identity must NOT be copied. Preserve my exact recognizable face shape, eyes, eyebrows, nose, lips, jawline, skin tone, natural facial features and age appearance. Do not beautify, reshape, slim, redesign, replace, age-change or mix my face with another person. No face swap, no identity mixing, no generic AI face. My natural identity must remain clearly recognizable as me.\n\nCreate a vertical 9:16 three-panel photographic collage, with three horizontal images stacked vertically and separated by thin dark gaps, matching the reference's intimate vintage editorial aesthetic.\n\nTOP PANEL: Close-up cropped portrait showing the lower half of the face, neck, shoulders and upper chest; the top of the head is intentionally outside the frame. Subject wears a clean white/off-white collared polo-style shirt with a soft cotton texture, subtle folds and naturally open collar. A very thin delicate chain necklace is visible around the neck. Face is turned slightly toward the right side, with only the lower face partially visible. Warm sunlight falls across the shirt and neck, creating soft bright highlights and gentle shadows. Background is dark, muted blue-gray/green architectural surroundings with a few vertical bright sunlit shapes, strongly blurred.\n\nMIDDLE PANEL: Extreme close-up of the subject's eyes and upper face, filling almost the entire frame horizontally. Thick dark slightly messy hair falls across the forehead. Strong natural eyebrows, realistic eyelashes, detailed eyes with warm dark-brown tones and small catchlights. Subject looks directly toward the camera with a calm, slightly serious expression. Preserve authentic skin texture around the eyes, subtle under-eye shadows and natural pores. Lighting is soft and warm, with one side slightly brighter and the opposite side gently shadowed. Keep the cinematic shallow-focus effect.\n\nBOTTOM PANEL: Close three-quarter portrait from approximately chest/shoulder level upward. Subject wears the same white/off-white collared shirt and thin chain necklace. Thick dark wavy hair falls naturally over the forehead and sides. Head tilted slightly downward and turned toward the right, eyes looking downward/off-camera. Calm, introspective expression. Jawline, cheek, nose and lips remain naturally visible. Warm directional sunlight illuminates one side of the face and neck while the opposite side falls into soft shadow. Background remains dark blue-gray and heavily blurred.\n\n🎨 COLOUR & FILTER\n\nMatch the exact visual mood: warm creamy whites, natural warm skin tones, muted blue-gray/dark green background, soft brown shadows and subtle golden highlights. Apply a vintage analog-film filter with slightly faded blacks, low-to-medium saturation, soft contrast, gentle warmth, creamy highlights and subtle grain. Keep whites slightly warm rather than pure cold white. No excessive orange tint or oversaturation.\n\n💡 LIGHTING & ATMOSPHERE\n\nUse soft natural sunlight coming from the side/front-side, producing warm highlights on the face, neck and white shirt. Shadows should be smooth, cinematic and slightly deep but retain facial detail. Create a nostalgic late-afternoon indoor/outdoor-window-light feeling with subtle haze and realistic light falloff. No harsh studio flash.\n\n📷 CAMERA & PHOTOGRAPHIC STYLE\n\nProfessional editorial portrait photography, intimate candid aesthetic, realistic full-frame camera rendering, approximately 50–85mm lens look, natural perspective, shallow depth of field, sharp facial details and softly blurred surroundings. Preserve realistic skin pores, individual hair strands, cotton fabric texture, necklace reflections and natural photographic imperfections. Subtle film grain and gentle optical softness.\n\nMaintain the exact three-panel arrangement and close-up framing, with each panel showing a different crop/angle while keeping the same person, white shirt, hairstyle, lighting and colour grading. The result should look like a genuine vintage editorial photo collage, not CGI or illustration.\n\n🚫 NEGATIVE PROMPT\n\nDifferent person, different identity, face swap, face replacement, generic AI face, identity mixing, altered facial proportions, beautified face, changed eyes, changed nose, changed lips, changed jawline, changed skin tone, age change, plastic skin, excessive smoothing, distorted eyes, unnatural hair, malformed anatomy, incorrect shirt colour, excessive saturation, excessive orange, harsh flash, HDR, CGI, cartoon, illustration, oversharpening, blurry face, low resolution, text, logo, watermark, extra people, duplicated features, incorrect collage layout.\n\nMOST IMPORTANT: Preserve my exact identity from my uploaded photo while recreating the reference's three-panel composition, white shirt, dark hair, eye close-up, side-profile pose, warm sunlight, dark blurred background, vintage filter, colours, grain and overall photographic character as accurately as possible."
